.TH KERO 1 "2026-08-20" "kero 0.1.0-alpha.1" "KERO User Manual"
.SH NAME
kero \- controls operations, policy, and environments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kero
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kero
manages KERO environments, resolves policy decisions, and provides artifact-bound Linux operation boundaries. It emits structured JSON for commands that report machine-readable results.
.PP
KERO has two independent environment types:
.TP
.B Global environment
A user-selected, machine-local environment for shared knowledge and policy. Initialize it with
.BR "kero init" .
.TP
.B Project environment
The nearest ancestor
.B .kero/
directory whose
.B kero.toml
declares a project environment. Initialize it with
.BR "kero project init" .
.PP
Global policy is not implicitly merged with project policy. When resolving a policy, pass each intended record file explicitly with
.BR "kero policy authorize --records" .
.SH INSTALLATION
Install from a source checkout by passing the CLI crate directory to Cargo:
.PP
.EX
cargo install --path /path/to/kero-source/code/kero-cli --locked
.EE
.PP
Cargo installs the executable into
.BR ~/.cargo/bin .
Ensure that directory is on
.BR PATH .
For fish:
.PP
.EX
fish_add_path ~/.cargo/bin
.EE
.PP
Install this manual page into the user manual path:
.PP
.EX
install -Dm644 docs/man/kero.1 ~/.local/share/man/man1/kero.1
man kero
.EE
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B kero init [--root PATH] [--skip-diagnostics] [--yes]
Run first-time global setup. In an interactive terminal, KERO checks local
storage and asks where to create the global environment. Supplying
.B --root
selects a location without prompting.
.TP
.B kero project init [--root PATH]
Create a project
.B .kero/
environment below
.IR PATH " (default: current directory)."
.TP
.B kero global init [--root PATH]
Create a global environment and save its location in the XDG KERO configuration. Without
.BR --root ,
the default is
.BR ~/.kero .
.TP
.B kero global path [--root PATH] [--plain]
Print the configured or explicitly supplied global environment and its identity.
.TP
.B kero project path [--start PATH] [--plain]
Walk upward from
.I PATH
to find the nearest project environment.
.TP
.B kero knowledge path {global|shared|local} [--start PATH] [--plain]
Print the selected knowledge location. The
.B global
area uses the global environment; the
.B shared
and
.B local
areas use the discovered project environment.
.TP
.B kero inspect [--start PATH]
Report global and project environment discovery independently. This is the recommended first diagnostic command.
.TP
.B kero policy authorize --request PATH [--environment PATH] [--records PATH]... [--snapshot-store PATH]
Load trusted policy records and produce an ALLOW or DENY decision plus an immutable snapshot. The default project paths are beneath
.BR .kero/policy/
and
.BR .kero/state/ .
.TP
.B kero policy replay --snapshot PATH --digest DIGEST --request PATH
Replay a request from an immutable policy snapshot without re-deciding policy.
.TP
.B kero verify-artifact OPTIONS
Verify a signed authorization artifact. Required options are
.BR --artifact ,
.BR --snapshot ,
.BR --key ,
.BR --audience ,
and
.BR --operation .
.TP
.B kero workspace-write OPTIONS
Perform one exact artifact-bound workspace write through the Linux broker.
.TP
.B kero bubblewrap OPTIONS -- ARGV...
Run one exact no-network command through Bubblewrap.
.TP
.B kero git-push OPTIONS
Push one exact non-force refspec with ambient Git credential helpers disabled.
.TP
.B kero https-service OPTIONS
Invoke one exact HTTPS destination using an explicitly resolved address.
.PP
Run
.B kero COMMAND --help
for complete option details for any command.
.SH GLOBAL DISCOVERY
KERO finds a global environment in this order:
.IP 1. 3
An explicit command root.
.IP 2. 3
The
.B KERO_GLOBAL_ROOT
environment variable.
.IP 3. 3
The configured root in
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kero/config.toml ,
or
.BR ~/.config/kero/config.toml .
.IP 4. 3
The fallback directory
.BR ~/.kero .
.PP
An environment must contain a compatible
.B kero.toml
with a
.B kero/global
or
.B kero/project
identity. Legacy Scope directories, including
.BR .scope/ ,
are not automatically adopted.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/kero/config.toml
Machine-local pointer to the selected global environment.
.TP
.B ~/.kero/
Default global environment location.
.TP
.B .kero/
Project-local KERO environment discovered by walking upward.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KERO_GLOBAL_ROOT
Overrides configured global-environment discovery.
.TP
.B KERO_CONFIG_HOME
Overrides the directory that contains
.BR config.toml .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Used when
.B KERO_CONFIG_HOME
is not set.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. A nonzero status indicates invalid input, failed discovery, failed policy resolution, failed artifact verification, or a boundary failure. Error results are emitted as JSON where applicable.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cargo (1),
.BR git (1)
